# Reflection

## What Copilot generated
GitHub Copilot helped generate parts of my Python functions, especially for loading the dataset and cleaning column names. I used comments to guide Copilot by describing what each function should do before writing the code, and used these comments as a part of my code to describe what is going on in the script. It also helped me with any errors I encountered along the way.

## What I modified
I changed several parts of Copilot’s output. For example, I updated variable names to match my dataset (such as using "qty" instead of "quantity"), since it wasn't recognizing the "quantity" string when running the code. I also improved the text cleaning logic to handle extra spaces and inconsistent formatting in product names and categories.

## What I learned
This assignment allowed me to learn how to clean up messy datasets, and how to neatly organize them based on any inconsistencies. I also learned that GitHub Copilot helps generate initial code that you can implement by just hitting tab, but you still shouldn't fully rely on it to make the code for you, as it can still create errors and still needs to be reviewed by a human.
